  "content": {
    "id": "p33-task26-29-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the angle of inclination of the following lines (to the nearest degree).",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-task26-29-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=2x+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$63^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Using $m=\\tan\\theta$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=2\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}(2)\\\\\\theta&\\approx63^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-task26-29-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p33-task26-29-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "153^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p33-task26-29-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The negative gradient gives an obtuse inclination: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\theta=180^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Inclination is measured anticlockwise from the positive $x$-axis, with $0^\\circ\\le\\theta<180^\\circ$. The negative gradient gives an obtuse inclination, supplementary to the acute angle found from its magnitude.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\\\theta&=180^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx153^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-task26-29-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3x-4y+8=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$37^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Using $m=\\tan\\theta$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{3}{4}x+2\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx37^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-task26-29-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$5x+2y-2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p33-task26-29-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "112^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p33-task26-29-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "m=-\\frac{5}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and the obtuse inclination ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\theta=180^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$y=-\\frac{5}{2}x+1$$\n\nInclination is measured anticlockwise from the positive $x$-axis, with $0^\\circ\\le\\theta<180^\\circ$. The negative gradient gives an obtuse inclination, supplementary to the acute angle found from its magnitude.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx112^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
